IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cma-types`
IMPORT `cma-definitions`
IMPORT `cma-offences`
IMPORT `cma-punishment`
IMPORT `cma-scope-procedure`
IMPORT `cma-goal`

-- Computer Misuse Act 1993 — INDEPENDENT TESTS.
--
-- Expected values are those fixed in independent-expectations.md, written from
-- BRIEF.md and ../source/CMA1993.txt before any encoding module was read.
-- Scenario ids (A1, B4, ...) refer to that file. Expected values are never
-- adjusted to match the encoding.

§ `Independent tests`

§§ `Helpers`

-- effect: altered, copied/moved, used data, executed, function of program, output, added, impaired
GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN, u IS A BOOLEAN, x IS A BOOLEAN, f IS A BOOLEAN, o IS A BOOLEAN, ad IS A BOOLEAN, im IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Effect on programs or data`
`fx` a c u x f o ad im MEANS `Effect on programs or data` WITH
    `altered or erased the program or data` IS a
    `copied or moved it to another storage medium or location` IS c
    `used the data` IS u
    `caused the program to be executed` IS x
    `was itself a function of the program` IS f
    `caused it to be output from the computer, in any form` IS o
    `added a program or data to the computer's contents` IS ad
    `impaired the normal operation of a computer, or contributed to it` IS im

`fx none`     MEANS `fx` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`fx altered`  MEANS `fx` TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`fx copied`   MEANS `fx` FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`fx executed` MEANS `fx` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`fx progfn`   MEANS `fx` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE FALSE
`fx shown`    MEANS `fx` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE FALSE
`fx added`    MEANS `fx` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE  FALSE
`fx impaired` MEANS `fx` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

GIVEN e IS A BOOLEAN, c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN Authority
`auth` e c MEANS Authority WITH
    `the person is entitled to control (or determine) access or modification of the kind` IS e
    `the person has consent from a person so entitled` IS c

`unauthorised` MEANS `auth` FALSE FALSE

GIVEN imp IS A BOOLEAN, loss IS A NUMBER, thr IS A MAYBE NUMBER, med IS A BOOLEAN, inj IS A BOOLEAN, pub IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Impairment facts`
`harm` imp loss thr med inj pub MEANS `Impairment facts` WITH
    `an impairment to a computer or to the integrity or availability of data, a program, a system or information` IS imp
    `loss caused, in dollars, within one year after the offence` IS loss
    `a different loss threshold prescribed by the Minister` IS thr
    `modifies or impairs, or potentially, medical examination, diagnosis, treatment or care` IS med
    `causes or threatens physical injury or death` IS inj
    `threatens public health or public safety` IS pub

GIVEN loss IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Impairment facts`
`loss of` loss MEANS `harm` TRUE loss NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN ex IS A `Device exclusion`
GIVETH A Device
`dev` ex MEANS Device WITH
    `is an electronic, magnetic, optical, electrochemical or other data processing device, or a group of them` IS TRUE
    `performs logical, arithmetic or storage functions` IS TRUE
    `exclusion` IS ex

GIVEN obtained IS A BOOLEAN, u IS A `Protected use`, knew IS A BOOLEAN, warned IS A BOOLEAN, rebutted IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Protected computer facts`
`pc` obtained u knew warned rebutted MEANS `Protected computer facts` WITH
    `access to the computer was obtained in the course of the offence` IS obtained
    `use` IS u
    `the accused knew, or ought reasonably to have known, of the use` IS knew
    `a warning of the enhanced penalty was exhibited to the accused` IS warned
    `the contrary of the presumed knowledge is proved` IS rebutted

`banking use` MEANS `(c) communications infrastructure, banking and financial services, public utilities, public transportation or public key infrastructure`
`no pc` MEANS `pc` FALSE `none of the s 11(2) uses` FALSE FALSE FALSE
`bank pc` MEANS `pc` TRUE `banking use` TRUE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN g IS A BOOLEAN, l IS A BOOLEAN, s IS A BOOLEAN, r IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `s 8A presumption facts`
`pres` g l s r MEANS `s 8A presumption facts` WITH
    `did the act for any gain, wrongful or not, realised or not, to anyone` IS g
    `did it knowing it is likely to cause wrongful loss` IS l
    `failed to take reasonable steps to ascertain the identity and physical location of the recipient` IS s
    `the contrary is proved` IS r

`no pres` MEANS `pres` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN k IS A BOOLEAN, o IS A BOOLEAN, used IS A BOOLEAN, steps IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Scam facts`
`scamf` k o used steps MEANS `Scam facts` WITH
    `knew the purpose or use was a scam offence` IS k
    `obtained or retained it for a scam offence, or for supply for one` IS o
    `proved to the court it was used for a scam offence` IS used
    `the accused proved reasonable steps against its use for a scam offence` IS steps

`no scamf` MEANS `scamf` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN d IS A `Dealing`, use IS A BOOLEAN, supply IS A BOOLEAN, knew IS A BOOLEAN, conduit IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Dealing facts`
`deal` d use supply knew conduit MEANS `Dealing facts` WITH
    `dealing` IS d
    `purpose: use in committing or facilitating an offence` IS use
    `purpose: supply or making available for use in an offence` IS supply
    `knew or had reason to believe it will be or is likely to be used for an offence` IS knew
    `merely provides network access, routing or connection services` IS conduit

`obt` MEANS `(a) obtains or retains`
`sup` MEANS `(b) supplies, offers to supply, transmits or makes available`

GIVEN prop IS A BOOLEAN, yrs IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Intended offence`
`intends` prop yrs MEANS `Intended offence` WITH
    `involves property, fraud or dishonesty, or causes bodily harm` IS prop
    `maximum imprisonment on conviction, in years` IS yrs

-- representative offences
`o3`  MEANS `s 3 unauthorised access to computer material` TRUE TRUE `fx shown` `unauthorised`
`o4`  MEANS `s 4 access with intent to commit an offence` TRUE `fx shown` (JUST (`intends` TRUE 5))
`o5`  MEANS `s 5 unauthorised modification of computer material` TRUE `fx added` `unauthorised`
`o6`  MEANS `s 6 unauthorised use or interception of computer service` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`o7`  MEANS `s 7 unauthorised obstruction of use of computer` TRUE TRUE FALSE
`o8`  MEANS `s 8 unauthorised disclosure of access code` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
GIVEN sc IS A `Scam facts`
GIVETH AN `Alleged offence`
`o8A with` sc MEANS `s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no pres` FALSE sc
`o8A` MEANS `o8A with` `no scamf`
GIVEN d IS A `Dealing`, sc IS A `Scam facts`
GIVETH AN `Alleged offence`
`o8B with` d sc MEANS `s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`deal` d TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) sc
`o8B` MEANS `o8B with` `obt` `no scamf`
`o9`  MEANS `s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`deal` `obt` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
`o10` MEANS `s 10 obtaining items for use in certain offences` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE

GIVEN o IS AN `Alleged offence`, rep IS A BOOLEAN, dmg IS A BOOLEAN, p IS A `Protected computer facts`, ind IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `CMA punishment`
`max` o rep dmg p ind MEANS `the maximum punishment for` o `, repeat:` rep `, damage caused:` dmg `, protected computer:` p `, an individual:` ind

GIVEN f IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER, c IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `CMA punishment`
`pun` f y c MEANS `CMA punishment` WITH `fine` IS f, `imprisonment in years` IS y, `caning strokes` IS c

GIVEN here IS A BOOLEAN, there IS A BOOLEAN, h IS A `Serious harm`
GIVETH A `Territorial facts`
`terr` here there h MEANS `Territorial facts` WITH
    `the accused was in Singapore at the material time` IS here
    `the computer, program or data was in Singapore at the material time` IS there
    `harm caused or significantly risked` IS h

`nh` MEANS `no serious harm in Singapore`

GIVEN p IS A STRING, c IS A STRING, d IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Act charged`
`act` p c d MEANS `Act charged` WITH
    `provision` IS p
    `computer` IS c
    `committed on` IS d

GIVEN d IS A DATE, o IS AN `Alleged offence`
GIVETH A Case
`case on` d o MEANS Case WITH
    `conduct on` IS d
    `alleged` IS o
    `participation` IS `as principal`
    `a second or subsequent conviction` IS FALSE
    `the offender is an individual` IS TRUE
    `damage` IS `loss of` 0
    `protected computer` IS `no pc`
    `territory` IS `terr` TRUE TRUE `nh`
    `prescribed as compoundable` IS TRUE

§§ `A. Definitions (s 2)`

-- A1-A6 s 2(1) "computer"
#ASSERT `a computer` (`dev` `not excluded`)
#ASSERT NOT `a computer` (`dev` `(a) an automated typewriter or typesetter`)
#ASSERT NOT `a computer` (`dev` `(b) a portable hand-held calculator`)
#ASSERT NOT `a computer` (`dev` `(c) a similar device which is non-programmable or has no data storage facility`)
#ASSERT NOT `a computer` (`dev` `(c) a similar device which is non-programmable or has no data storage facility`)
#ASSERT NOT `a computer` (`dev` `(d) a device the Minister has prescribed by Gazette notification`)
-- A7-A13 s 2(2)-(3)
#ASSERT `secures access to a program or data` `fx altered`
#ASSERT `secures access to a program or data` `fx copied`
#ASSERT `secures access to a program or data` `fx copied`
#ASSERT `secures access to a program or data` `fx shown`
#ASSERT `secures access to a program or data` `fx executed`
#ASSERT `secures access to a program or data` `fx progfn`
#ASSERT NOT `secures access to a program or data` `fx none`
-- A14-A16 s 2(5)
#ASSERT `without authority` `unauthorised`
#ASSERT NOT `without authority` (`auth` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `without authority` (`auth` TRUE FALSE)
-- A17-A20 s 2(7)
#ASSERT `a modification of the contents of a computer` `fx altered`
#ASSERT `a modification of the contents of a computer` `fx added`
#ASSERT `a modification of the contents of a computer` `fx impaired`
#ASSERT NOT `a modification of the contents of a computer` `fx none`
-- A21-A22 s 2(8)
#ASSERT `without authority` (`auth` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `without authority` (`auth` FALSE TRUE)
-- A23-A31 s 2(1) "damage"
#ASSERT `damage` (`loss of` 10000)
#ASSERT NOT `damage` (`loss of` 9999.99)
-- A25: only the $6,000 within one year may be counted (the later $6,000 is excluded)
#ASSERT NOT `damage` (`loss of` 6000)
-- A26: $4,000 + $7,000 aggregate
#ASSERT `damage` (`loss of` (4000 PLUS 7000))
#ASSERT `damage` (`harm` TRUE 0 NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `damage` (`harm` TRUE 0 NOTHING FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `damage` (`harm` TRUE 0 NOTHING FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `damage` (`harm` FALSE 50000 NOTHING FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `damage` (`harm` TRUE 15000 (JUST 20000) FALSE FALSE FALSE)

§§ `B. Offences (ss 3-10, 12)`

-- B1-B3 s 3
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `o3`
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 3 unauthorised access to computer material` FALSE TRUE `fx shown` `unauthorised`)
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 3 unauthorised access to computer material` TRUE TRUE `fx shown` (`auth` FALSE TRUE))
-- B4-B8 s 4; B4 authorised access is immaterial (s 4(4)(a)) — the s 4 type takes no authority at all
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `o4`
#ASSERT `an offence to which s 4 applies` (`intends` TRUE 2)
#ASSERT NOT `an offence to which s 4 applies` (`intends` TRUE 1)
#ASSERT NOT `an offence to which s 4 applies` (`intends` FALSE 10)
#ASSERT `an offence to which s 4 applies` (`intends` TRUE 3)
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 4 access with intent to commit an offence` TRUE `fx shown` (JUST (`intends` TRUE 1)))
-- B9-B10 s 5
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `o5`
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 5 unauthorised modification of computer material` TRUE `fx added` (`auth` FALSE TRUE))
-- B11-B12 s 6
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `o6`
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 6 unauthorised use or interception of computer service` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- B13-B14 s 7
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `o7`
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 7 unauthorised obstruction of use of computer` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- B15-B16 s 8
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `o8`
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8 unauthorised disclosure of access code` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- B17-B22 s 8A
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `o8A`
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` FALSE TRUE TRUE `no pres` FALSE `no scamf`)
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`pres` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE `no scamf`)
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`pres` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE) FALSE `no scamf`)
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` TRUE TRUE FALSE (`pres` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) FALSE `no scamf`)
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8A disclosure in relation to the national digital identity service` TRUE TRUE TRUE `no pres` TRUE `no scamf`)
-- B23-B27 s 8B
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `o8B`
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`deal` `obt` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `no scamf`)
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`deal` `sup` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `no scamf`)
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`deal` `sup` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `no scamf`)
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 8B dealing in another person's credential` TRUE (`deal` `sup` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) `no scamf`)
-- B28-B34 s 9 and its Examples
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `o9`
-- Example 1, (1)(a): A downloads/retains for reporting to police
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`deal` `obt` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- Example 1, (1)(b): A transmits to B, no knowledge or reason to believe of misuse
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`deal` `sup` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- Example 2: C transmits to D for B's investigation
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`deal` `sup` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
-- B32: variant, C had reason to believe D would misuse
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`deal` `sup` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- B33: obtained by a s 7 contravention only: no knowledge of a s 3/4/5/6 contravention
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` FALSE TRUE (`deal` `obt` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 9 dealing in personal information obtained by a computer offence` TRUE TRUE (`deal` `sup` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE))
-- B35-B36 s 10
#ASSERT `the elements are made out` `o10`
#ASSERT NOT `the elements are made out` (`s 10 obtaining items for use in certain offences` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- B37 s 12
#ASSERT `is guilty of the offence itself, with its punishment` `by abetment`
#ASSERT `is guilty of the offence itself, with its punishment` `by attempt`

§§ `C. Punishment (ss 3-11; caning)`

#ASSERT `max` `o3` FALSE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 5000 2 0
#ASSERT `max` `o3` TRUE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 10000 3 0
#ASSERT `max` `o3` FALSE TRUE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 50000 7 0
#ASSERT `max` `o3` TRUE TRUE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 50000 7 0
#ASSERT `max` `o4` FALSE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 50000 10 0
#ASSERT `max` `o4` TRUE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 50000 10 0
#ASSERT `max` `o5` FALSE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 10000 3 0
#ASSERT `max` `o5` TRUE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 20000 5 0
#ASSERT `max` `o6` FALSE TRUE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 50000 7 0
#ASSERT `max` `o7` TRUE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 20000 5 0
#ASSERT `max` `o8` TRUE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 20000 5 0
#ASSERT `max` `o8` FALSE TRUE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 10000 3 0
#ASSERT `max` `o8A` FALSE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 10000 3 0
#ASSERT `max` `o8A` TRUE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 10000 3 0
#ASSERT `max` `o8B` TRUE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 20000 5 0
#ASSERT `max` `o9` FALSE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 10000 3 0
#ASSERT `max` `o10` TRUE FALSE `no pc` TRUE EQUALS `pun` 20000 5 0
-- C18-C21 s 11(1)
